<p id="p2">The Magic Keyboard isn’t the only accessory Apple updated today. <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/08/25/apple-40w-dynamic-power-adapter-europe/" rel="noopener noreferrer">As Juli Clover reports for MacRumors</a>, the 40W Dynamic Power Adapter that can charge up to 60W was also updated for users in Europe and Vietnam:</p>
<blockquote id="blockquote3"><p>
  The updated variant of the power adapter has a retractable two-prong design. The prongs pop back into the power adapter’s enclosure, making it easier to tuck into a bag or a pocket. Apple previously debuted a standard U.S. variant in September 2025 alongside the <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/iphone-17/" rel="noopener noreferrer">iPhone 17</a> models, and a <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2025/11/13/apple-40w-dynamic-power-adapter/" rel="noopener noreferrer">type G plug version</a> in November 2025.
</p></blockquote>
<div class="media-wrapper"><img decoding="async" src="https://cdn.macstories.net/images/uploads/2026/08/25/untitled-19-1787701607486-b9646746c5.jpg" alt="At this price, why not buy two?"><p class="image-caption">At this price, why not buy two?</p></div>
<p id="p5">Plus, as <a href="https://9to5mac.com/2026/08/25/apple-releases-new-polishing-cloth-for-9/" rel="noopener noreferrer">Chance Miller covered for 9to5Mac</a>, there’s a new Apple Polishing Cloth. It’s not clear whether the new cloth is different from the one that came before it, but in one respect it’s a big improvement. The updated Polishing Cloth has dropped in price to $9 from $19. In a world of high-priced memory and storage, I’ll take the pricing wins where I can get them.</p>
